Reason: The provided `AtomicThrowable` class is a thin utility wrapper around `AtomicReference` with straightforward delegation to other RxJava components. Its methods perform minimal logic (atomic updates, simple condition checks) and rely heavily on external classes (`ExceptionHelper`, `RxJavaPlugins`). Benchmarking such trivial operations would not yield meaningful performance insights, and setting up realistic JMH tests would require extensive mocking of the RxJava infrastructure, which is beyond the scope of a simple microbenchmark. Therefore, generating JMH benchmark code is unnecessary.